t a commensurate increase in hidden complexity. Each new surface point is a coupling tax on every caller; justify it. If removing the new export would force callers to duplicate 3+ branches or non-inlineable control flow, it is deep; if callers could inline it in one line, it is shallow. Facade and adapter modules, and idiomatic or framework-required patterns where thin delegation is the convention — for example, TypeScript barrel re-exports (`index.ts`), Python `__init__.py` re-exports, Next.js route handlers, or Rust trait impls — are not shallow-module violations.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
